`test_selected_recording_v2.py` uses temporary text metadata fixtures, with maker inventory and PNG validation explicitly mocked. It invokes the actual new preparer, uses its exact job/prompt/raw packet schema, runs the real adapter through a shell, and validates three synthetic CLI metadata records plus explicit archive-reader replay. Synthetic session IDs and CLI events are clearly labeled fixture data; no critic session is launched. Both initial and selected fixture chains have all source/poster visits false, mandatory judgments NA, and all score/diversity values null. Valid recording bindings therefore do not claim usable viewing or visual quality.

